Root cause:
The root cause of the bug was that the `task_struct` associated with the resource tracking object was acquired but not released, leading to a resource leak. This occurred because the call to `rdma_restrack_del()` was incorrectly placed after the resource associated with `id_priv` was freed, which meant that the resource tracking object was not properly cleaned up, resulting in the leak. The patch corrects this by moving the call to `rdma_restrack_del()` to ensure that the resource is released before the associated memory is freed.
